      "source_sha256": "sha256:9bf0093cc42422d29b742c08d3d1976e6bcc149458a75c712b3593a19739ee6c",
      "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:omit. vb (tr) , omits, omitting or omitted. 1. to neglect to do or include. 2. to fail (to do something). [C15: from Latin omittere, from ob-away + mittere to send]. (o\u028a\u02c8m\u026at). v.t. o\u2022mit\u2022ted, o\u2022mit\u2022ting.\\n\\npassage 2:verb. erase, remove. 1  X-out. 2  annul. 3  black out. 4  bleep. 5  blot out. 6  blue-pencil. 7  cancel. 8  clean. 9  clean up. 10  cross out. 11  cut. 12  cut out. 13  decontaminate. 14  destroy. 15  drop. 16  edit. 17  efface. 18  eliminate. 19  exclude. 20  expunge. 21  obliterate. 22  omit. 23  pass up. 24  rub. 25  rub out. 26  rule out. 27  sanitize. 28  snip. 29  squash. 30  squelch. 31  sterilize. 32  strike out. 33  trim. 34  wipe out.\\n\\npassage 3:Hotels often omit to check guests' cars \u2192 Les hotels h\u00f4tels omettent souvent de verifier v\u00e9rifier les voitures. Des clients he omitted to say whether these men would \u2192 Be armed il a omis de dire si ces hommes allaient. etre \u00eatre armes arm\u00e9s\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"synonym for omit\"}",
